# >>> claude-dash
# Size and position are NOT set here on purpose: this rule fires the moment the
# window is mapped, and foot then applies its own default geometry over the top,
# so a `resize set` here is silently lost. claude-dash-toggle sizes and centres
# the window after showing it instead (see CLAUDE_DASH_WIDTH / _HEIGHT).
# A user sway config REPLACES /etc/sway/config rather than extending it, so a
# config that never sets floating_modifier leaves every floating window
# undraggable. Restore the distro default: Super+left-drag moves, right-drag
# resizes. Drop this line if your config already sets it.
floating_modifier $mod normal
for_window [app_id="claude-dash"] floating enable, move scratchpad
# <<< claude-dash
